Dutch Station Addition Set v0.8
-----------------------------------

Contents:

1 About
2 Requirements
3 Installation
4 Usage
5 License
6 Credits




-------
1 About
-------

The DSA-set is a station set that can help you create Dutch style stations and waypoints.
Initially the idea was to convert the original Dutch Station set into island style platforms. But more and more idea's followed and were also incorporated in this GRF.
See development thread for more information and screenshots: http://www.tt-forums.net/viewtopic.php?f=26&t=64121#p1063214

Dutch Station Addition Set v0.8
Name: dstatadd_v0_8.grf
Version:  0.8
GRF ID:   50 4A 01 10





--------------
2 Requirements
--------------

Recommended is to use the latest (nightly)release of OpenTTD. Also this set will look at it's best when combined with the Total Bridge Renewal set and the Metro Track Set.



--------------
3 Installation
--------------

Copy the DSA-set .grf file to the OpenTTD data directory. The OpenTTD readme explains where you can find this directory.

The final step is to activate the DSA station tiles.
This is done via the NewGRF Settings window, which is explained here:
http://wiki.openttd.org/NewGRF.
Now you can use the DSA stations in your new games.



-------
4 Usage
-------

These stationtiles can be used to create Dutch style stations and waypoints.



---------
5 License
---------

DSA-set for OpenTTD
Copyright (C) 2013 Quast65

